      "id": "1ij8m5j",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Extraction of Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Sodium and Potassium are soft metals that can be cut with a knife and must be stored in kerosene to prevent reaction with moisture.",
        "Mercury is the only liquid metal at room temperature, whereas Bromine is the only liquid non-metal.",
        "Amphoteric oxides like Aluminium Oxide (Al2O3) and Zinc Oxide (ZnO) react with both acids and bases to produce salt and water.",
        "Aqua Regia (3:1 ratio of concentrated HCl and concentrated HNO3) can dissolve noble metals like Gold and Platinum."
      ],
      "id": "r31cgu0"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "byjojee",
      "content": "• Highly reactive metals are extracted by electrolysis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w0n1zsr",
      "content": "• Moderately reactive metals are extracted by reduction using carbon."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "smwjzzq",
      "content": "• Less reactive metals are often found in free state."
    },
    {
      "id": "5xr1g4c",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pcq380k",
      "content": "• Metals are good conductors of heat and electricity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i32cayi",
      "content": "• Non-metals are generally poor conductors."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zynk6wz",
      "content": "• Mercury is the only metal that is liquid at room temperature."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "svyx3cg",
      "content": "• Gold and silver are least reactive metals."
    }
  ],
